# Terraform — append to the repo .gitignore, or keep as terraform/.gitignore

# Provider binaries and module cache. Large (a single provider runs to hundreds of MB)
# and re-downloadable.
**/.terraform/*

# .terraform.lock.hcl is deliberately NOT ignored: provider versions are part of the
# build, and a lock file that is not committed pins nothing.

# State and its backups. State holds resource IDs and can hold secret values in plain
# text; it belongs in the remote backend. These lines guard a stray local run.
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfplan
crash.log
crash.*.log

# Terraform's override convention, for local experiments that must not ship.
override.tf
override.tf.json
*_override.tf
*_override.tf.json

# CLI credentials.
.terraformrc
terraform.rc

# NOTE: *.tfvars is deliberately NOT ignored. A tfvars file holds identifiers —
# subscription id, tenant id, object ids — and never secrets; secrets live in the
# key store and are set out of band. Ignoring tfvars would HIDE a leaked secret
# rather than prevent one. Committed and reviewable is the stronger position: if a
# tfvars ever needs a secret, that is the bug, not this line.
